id: pm-lint-qcob
title: Install the pinned release npm into a job-local prefix
description: "The release workflow replaces the runner's global npm with the pinned npm. Parallel jobs on one runner host share the toolcache Node installation, so one job's global install mutates a sibling job's npm mid-install (ENOTEMPTY, or npm: command not found), as reported by unbraind/pm-ops#284 for the fleet."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-lint#92","gh:unbraind/pm-ops#284"
created_at: "2026-11-16T14:41:56.962Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T15:44:13.153Z"
author: pi-glm
acceptance_criteria: The release workflow installs the pinned npm with --prefix into a job-local directory and prepends that prefix bin to the job path; The workflow keeps the exact-version assertion on the effective npm; A workflow-contract test fails if any workflow replaces the global npm
comments[34]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T15:17:30.403Z",codex-sol,"Continuation: verified the existing worktree and remote branch state, preserved the earlier changes, and reused this item. Rerunning required gates to completion under the continuation author before committing results."
  "2026-11-16T15:28:18.044Z",codex-sol,"Root cause confirmed in the workflow source: global installation of the pinned npm replaces the same Node installation used by parallel jobs on a shared toolcache. Replaced each bootstrap with a job-local prefix, published only its bin directory to the job PATH, and retained exact-pin checks including a separate subsequent-step assertion. Workflow contracts reject global npm replacement across all workflow files. No runner settings or shared tool installations were modified."
  "2026-11-16T15:42:15.343Z",codex-sol,The first combined gate command hit its 20-minute timeout during shared-host disk contention and is not pass evidence. Retrying all gates to completion using memory-backed temporary fixtures and the existing harness deadline scale. Assertions and test selection are unchanged.
  "2026-11-16T15:57:52.477Z",codex-sol,"Workflow contracts passed. changelog:check then correctly required the new in-progress item in the generated changelog; regenerated it with the package generator and verified the diff is limited to this item entry. Rechecking the contracts and changelog together."
  "2026-11-16T16:02:00.880Z",codex-sol,"Before publication: typecheck and lint completed successfully. The focused workflow contract suite passed 33 tests, and changelog:check passed after generating the required in-progress item entry. The first full quick test command timed out under disk contention; its replacement is active and remains pending evidence. Publishing a draft for exact-head CI validation."
  "2026-11-16T16:11:55.188Z",codex-sol,"Implementation commit c9cdd8267c642641d175b2c9a8bb227231982f36 contains the requested fix and package-owned regression contracts. Focused contracts and changelog verification passed; typecheck and lint or the existing docstring static gate passed. The first broad quick attempt timed out, and its replacement remains active. The shared runner dispatch hold is respected before publication. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-16T16:47:55.534Z",codex-sol,"The broad local retry reached its 60-minute command limit before completion; the repairs acceptance did not complete successfully. Typecheck, lint, all 33 focused workflow contracts and changelog:check passed separately. The broad suite remains an explicit validation gap. Tracking PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/92. The PR remains open for orchestrator verification; exact-head CI is queued or running."
  "2026-11-16T19:23:54.337Z",codex-sol,"Review round P: replace the workflow-wide regex with a dependency-free shell command parser and regression fixtures. Parse run scripts with existing yaml where available; preserve allowed prefix-local installs. Verify typecheck, lint or docstring, focused guard/workflow contracts and changelog checks before pushing. No review-thread actions."
  "2026-11-16T19:28:33.450Z",codex-sol,"Review round P addresses PR #92 (no existing review thread): shared-npm replacement guard now tokenizes shell commands and uses existing yaml for run scripts. Added 38 fixtures covering npm aliases, flag placement/location, package specs, continuations, quotes/paths, separators and allowed installs. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint and npm run changelog:check PASS. The new linked guard and workflow contracts passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress: 71 pass, 0 fail/cancel/skip/todo. Full-suite certification is left to CI; review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-17T01:51:22.030Z",codex-sol,"Review round AA: pulled and verified the open PR head. Source inspection confirms the reported guard gaps. Replace shell tokenization with conservative logical-line matching and step-only script extraction, with intended false positives and regression fixtures."
  "2026-11-17T02:02:11.938Z",codex-sol,"All three scoped threads verified valid: PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64LT7m, PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64LT7o, PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64LT7r. Replaced the tokenizer with conservative logical-line matching; the existing direct YAML dependency now collects only jobs.*.steps[*].run. Regression fixtures cover ampersands, assignments, npx, conditionals, groups, scoped operands, folded scalars, metadata isolation and unreadable values. Guard plus release-approval suite: 86 passed. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, duplication and changelog:check passed through the targeted PM gate. All real workflows passed. No dependencies added; no findings refused. Full-suite certification remains with CI."
  "2026-11-17T03:37:18.498Z",pi-claude,"Round AF follow-up on the fail-closed guard, from review threads pm-lint PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn2, PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn6 and PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn7 (the same three findings were raised on the pm-ado threads and replicate in every fleet copy of this guard; this repository's workflowGlobalNpmInstalls uses the direct YAML dependency). All three findings were reproduced against the guard source first: a prefix bootstrap followed by '&& npm install -g npm@11.19.0', 'npm install -gpld npm@11.19.0' and step env NPM_CONFIG_GLOBAL=true were all accepted by the previous code.\n\n1. Segment-scoped prefix exception: run scripts now split into command segments at unquoted ;, &, | and newlines. The scanner tracks quote state across lines and $( … ) substitutions (which nest a fresh quoting context even inside double quotes), skips comments and here-document bodies, and any script that cannot be delimited (unbalanced quote or substitution) fails closed as 'undelimitable command line'. The job-local prefix exception only covers the segment carrying it; rejected fixtures add 'npm install --prefix \"$RUNNER_TEMP/npm-11.19.0\" npm@11.19.0 && npm install -g npm@11.19.0' and 'npm install --prefix \"$RUNNER_TEMP/npm-local\" npm@11.19.0; npm install -g npm@11.19.0'. Approved bootstrap fixtures stay accepted.\n2. Combined short flags: any single-dash letter cluster containing g now marks global (rejected: 'npm install -gpld npm@11.19.0', 'npm install -dg npm@11.19.0'); 'npm install -D pnpm' and 'npm install -gpld pnpm' stay accepted.\n3. Workflow, job and step env compose for each step run, the step scope taking precedence; npm reads npm_config_* keys case-insensitively. npm_config_global set to anything other than false/0/empty, npm_config_location=global, a ${{ … }} expression value, or an unreadable env scope or entry forces every npm install in that run global unless its own segment carries a job-local prefix. Fixtures cover step env flow mapping, job env flow and block styles, workflow env, expression values, location=global, step-override (job \"true\" + step \"false\" accepted) and accepted \"false\"/\"0\"/\"\" values.\n\nGates: guard suite 62 passed; release-approval suite 33 passed; typecheck (including the test project), lint, duplication and changelog:check passed. Every workflow in the repository still scans clean. Full-suite certification remains with CI."
  "2026-11-17T05:22:27.626Z",codex-sol,"Round AH: implement conservative run-wide global configuration and markers, install-family aliases, redirect-safe prefix segmentation, and comment-free effective prefix exemptions. Preserve all existing rejected fixtures and approved bootstrap workflows; verify required package gates before releasing the claim. No review-thread mutations."
  "2026-11-17T05:29:48.960Z",codex-sol,"Round AH verification: 135 tests passed with zero failures, cancellations or skips (102 guard fixtures plus release-approval contracts). npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run lint, npm run duplication, npm run identity:check, npm run changelog:check and git diff --check all passed. The same Round AH fixes are applied as in the companion npm-guard PRs. All earlier rejected fixtures are retained; approved bootstraps and repository workflows pass. Global signals are run-wide, and only effective command arguments can establish a prefix exemption. Shared guard logic matches all four copies. Protected item dates are unchanged. Exact-head CI remains pending; no thread actions, publishing or merges."
  "2026-11-17T07:45:11.894Z",pi-guard-1117aj,"Round AJ (thread PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64SxPd): replaced the guard's per-segment shell parser with a line-based fail-closed rule, identical to the other fleet repositories: logical lines only (continuations joined, newline-only splits), comment and here-document text scanned like any other text, install family extended with update/up/upgrade/udpate, markers covering single-dash g clusters, global-containing tokens, -L with any value and two-plus-letter prefixes of global/location, npm config set/set as a run-wide global signal (narrowed to a set token because the release workflow's read-only 'npm config get globalconfig' tripped), operands naming npm by substring or computed form, exemptions restricted to exact approved bootstrap lines, and step-level rejection of GITHUB_ENV npm_config_* writes and global/location npmrc writes. The release-approval test now also asserts the bootstrap appends the same prefix's node_modules/.bin to $GITHUB_PATH and that the Verify job-local npm version step expects exactly the installed version. One run comment was reworded because it read like the forbidden command."
  "2026-11-17T08:23:17.362Z",codex-sol,"Round AM verified against unchanged guard: punctuation and comment-continuation bypasses, operandless global installs, persistent npm config setters, and spaced YAML env keys reproduce. Quoted command words already reject; add explicit regression coverage. Keep line-based checks and exact raw-line bootstrap matching. Unresolved review threads: PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGc, PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGg, PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGj. Delegated npx finding is already rejected by Round AJ; preserve its rejected fixture. Run targeted gates directly; never execute linked PM tests. Preserve the existing test-session isolation import in the pm-vcs fixture."
  "2026-11-17T08:29:08.399Z",codex-sol,"Round AM targeted verification: 186 tests passed with zero failures, cancellations or skips. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-approval.test.ts => PASS; npm run typecheck => PASS; npm run lint => PASS; npm run changelog:check => PASS. Scripts absent: duplicates. All real workflows pass the guard; no bootstrap trailing comment was found. Guard source md5 d7ec9edd85b0c9fbe3d5a9f0e4d8d9e2 is identical across five packages. Fixture bodies match, retaining the required pm-vcs session-isolation import. Protected root item dates are unchanged; rejected fixtures are preserved. Same-class config persistence and spaced YAML env-key fixes from PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGg, PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64U3xi and PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGj were applied to every copy. Full-suite certification remains with CI. Releasing this claim without closing the item."
  "2026-11-17T08:42:16.747Z",codex-sol,"Round AN: inspect unresolved review threads; scan joined and physical lines independently and union findings, with exact bootstrap exemptions local to each form. Preserve all fixtures and add quoted-hash regressions. Run the requested package gates directly; do not execute linked PM tests."
  "2026-11-17T08:46:59.792Z",codex-sol,"Round AN verified: none unresolved. Joined and physical scans union findings; exact bootstrap exemptions apply per form. All old fixtures retained; four quoted-hash cases plus LF/CRLF union/exemption/dedup checks added. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-approval.test.ts: 191/191 pass, zero skipped. npm run typecheck and npm run changelog:check: pass. npm run lint and npm run duplication: pass, 0% duplicated. Guard md5: 9472ab1dff99c26c27085f766054f46d. Review threads were read only; lifecycle timestamps preserved."
  "2026-11-17T09:01:35.683Z",codex-sol,"Round AP: reject every global update/up/upgrade/udpate line regardless of operands; option values, redirect targets and comment words cannot hide an update. Install-family operand handling stays unchanged. Preserve all prior fixtures, add the five requested rejections and alias/global-environment coverage, then run the Round AN gates directly. All five PRs remain open. No review-thread mutations."
  "2026-11-17T09:02:59.692Z",codex-sol,"Round AP verification: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-approval.test.ts => PASS; npm run typecheck => PASS; npm run lint => PASS; npm run changelog:check => PASS; git diff --check => PASS. Focused suite: ℹ tests 197, ℹ pass 197, ℹ fail 0, ℹ cancelled 0, ℹ skipped 0, ℹ todo 0. Every real workflow still passes; all prior fixtures retained. Guard md5 e882f7b9396d4a810ccf85250dc05a04. No configured duplicates script."
  "2026-11-17T10:20:47.033Z",codex-sol,"Round AR: reproduced assignment-valued short-flag, renamed-archive, quoted-expression and uppercase Boolean bypasses against the unchanged shared guard. Preserve dual line scans and all fixtures; replace global operand inference with a registry-spec allowlist, normalize option names before marker tests and compare env values exactly. Run the round AN gates and regenerate changelog after all tracker writes. Leave this item open."
  "2026-11-17T10:25:39.598Z",codex-sol,"Round AR implementation and validation: PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64Xsnl. Global install operands now require the plain registry name-spec allowlist and exclude npm identities; archive, path, URL, git, alias, computed and quote-fragment operands reject. Option names are unquoted and split before assignment-valued marker tests. Env keys ignore case but safe global/location values compare exactly, including run assignments. Both physical and joined scans and bootstrap exemptions remain. Preserved all prior fixtures; focused guard: 202/202; round AN contract gate: 235/235; typecheck passed. All real workflows pass the guard. Guard md5: 1b36b35bf3ce5df79ae313b939f17971. Lint and duplication gates passed with zero clones. Identity gate passed. Corrected a fixture-only inferred union type before the passing typecheck. Final tracker writes precede tag refresh and changelog regeneration/check; keep the item in_progress and release the claim. No review thread mutations or workflow dispatches."
  "2026-11-17T10:52:48.899Z",codex-sol,"Round AS: verified current code before editing. The line union omits PowerShell backticks and the workflow extractor omits container and service env scopes. Add LF/CRLF and effective-env regressions, preserve all existing fixtures, and keep all five guard copies identical."
  "2026-11-17T10:59:30.521Z",codex-sol,"Round AS: addressed the shared findings PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64YXiD and PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64YXiL from pm-ops#289. Verified both bypasses against the previous guard; new fixtures failed before fixes and pass after them. Scan the union of normalized physical lines, joined backslashes and joined PowerShell backticks, with LF/CRLF fixtures. Compose container defaults with workflow/job/step scopes; conservatively check service env scopes independently so one safe service cannot mask another unsafe service. Unsupported container env fails closed. Retained all approved/rejected fixtures and real workflow checks. No equivalent overlapping-install test exists here. Main gates passed 237/237; additional tooling references 35/35; build and typecheck passed; lint, duplication and identity checks passed. All five guard copies have md5 a515dca0fd6175db9bcb1dc5c780989c. No findings refused. Changelog generation/check follows final tracker writes; CI is not yet verified."
  "2026-11-17T13:53:44.266Z",codex-sol,"Round AV: reproduced command-prefix/camelCase, Cmd continuation and indentationless job-list defects with failing regressions. Checked npm 11.21.0 packaged command/alias definitions; retain conservative prefix scanning, physical/joined union and operand allowlist. Audit found no optional npm setup followed by unconditional verification in this repository."
  "2026-11-17T13:57:45.193Z",codex-sol,"Round AV verified results: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/package-metadata.test.ts test/release-approval.test.ts test/tooling.test.ts PASS (1/1/0/0/0 tests/pass/fail/cancelled/skipped); npm run typecheck PASS; npm run lint PASS; npm run duplication PASS; Initial workflow scan flagged three prose comments because a is now a valid family prefix. Reworded those comments without weakening comment scanning; expanded reference-based suite and every real workflow now pass.. Changelog regeneration/check follows these final tracker writes. Item remains in progress for orchestrator review."
  "2026-11-17T14:51:17.296Z",codex-sol,"Round AW: verifying four shared guard findings before edits: continuation forms must scan separately, link/ln can have implicit global effects, --g denotes global mode, and multiline npmrc writes must be checked against all run contents. Keep the line-based guard identical across all five packages, preserve existing fixtures, and run workflow/reference gates. No new tracker items or closures."
  "2026-11-17T15:07:56.259Z",codex-sol,"Round AW: reproduced all four findings against the unchanged guard, including the two-step npmrc workflow. Addresses PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864eCYU, PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864eYv2, PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64esLn, PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64esLy. The line-based guard now unions physical lines and three independent joins, applies the registry operand allowlist to implicit link/ln effects (including bare links), accepts one-letter global option prefixes, and checks npmrc writes against the whole run. Preserved every existing fixture; added accepted non-npm registry links and npmrc writes with no global/location mention. Guard MD5 02f427a1776c5b99d68b1c10b03a3939. Verified: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-approval.test.ts PASS (266/266/0/0/0 tests/pass/fail/cancelled/skipped); npm run typecheck PASS; npm run lint PASS; npm run duplication PASS; npm run build PASS; node --test test/install.acceptance.ts PASS (1/1/0/0/0 tests/pass/fail/cancelled/skipped). All five PRs were open and mergeable; the pm-slack unresolved-thread read had no findings. Final changelog generation/check follows these tracker writes. Item remains in progress for orchestrator review."
  "2026-11-17T15:10:48.775Z",codex-sol,"Round AW post-push state check found the PR conflicting with updated main. Integrate origin/main as a separate merge commit; the conflict is the generated changelog. Incoming main includes source, dependency, metadata and caller-test updates, so refresh locked dependencies and rerun the affected package suites, typecheck, lint, duplication, build and installed npm/Bun acceptance. Preserve the shared guard bytes and existing item timestamps. Regenerate/check CHANGELOG.md after these final tracker writes, then explicitly stage the merge paths; do not fold the merge into the guard code commit."
  "2026-11-17T15:29:22.025Z",codex-sol,"Round AW updated-main validation complete: refreshed locked dependencies with npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund. npm test passed all 444 tests with zero failures, cancellations or skips at full model depth; npm run typecheck, npm run lint and npm run duplication passed. node --test test/install.acceptance.ts passed the packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx consumers against the updated source/toolchain. The independently scheduled acceptance and complete unit suites retained their assertions and full model depth. Keep the upstream source/toolchain integration in its own merge commit; shared guard MD5 remains 02f427a1776c5b99d68b1c10b03a3939. Regenerate/check the changelog after these final tracker writes, preserve incoming main tracker records unchanged, and leave this item in progress for orchestrator review."
  "2026-11-17T15:37:27.343Z",codex-sol,"Round AW late review PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64gC3N: reproduced empty findings for npm link --loglevel warn, npm ln --loglevel warn, and a command-looking option value before link. Option values must not masquerade as package operands for implicit links. Keep the scanner line-based: accept inline option values and known boolean global flags, but reject ambiguous unbound link options conservatively, including shell punctuation hidden in an option token. Existing accepted link -g some-tool remains accepted; added accepted inline-option registry links and rejected bare/options/punctuation regressions. Recheck the affected AN/reference suites and quality gates, then finalize tracker/changelog/source and regenerate the final self-host archive where required."
  "2026-11-17T15:38:19.308Z",codex-sol,"Round AW PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64gC3N verified: every existing fixture remains, new link-option and punctuation regressions reject, and known boolean global/inline-value registry links remain accepted. Full line-based guard MD5 23618780bdf981d6734941c1d5accb2e. Final affected gates: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-approval.test.ts PASS (276/276/0/0/0 tests/pass/fail/cancelled/skipped); npm run typecheck PASS; npm run lint PASS; npm run duplication PASS. Production package source and manifests did not change in this follow-up; prior expanded reference and real npm/Bun acceptance results remain applicable. Final tracker writes precede changelog regeneration/check. Leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-17T15:44:10.408Z",codex-sol,"Round AW PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64gC3N final refinement: read-only npm config queries confirmed that -g false and --g false consume a boolean option value. Empty inline values also fail closed. Verified: every existing fixture remains, new link-option and punctuation regressions reject, and known boolean global/inline-value registry links remain accepted. Full line-based guard MD5 0055f72ef4fb208809848324cb902d9a. Final affected gates: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-approval.test.ts PASS (281/281/0/0/0 tests/pass/fail/cancelled/skipped); npm run typecheck PASS; npm run lint PASS; npm run duplication PASS. Production package source and manifests did not change in this follow-up; prior expanded reference and real npm/Bun acceptance results remain applicable. Final tracker writes precede changelog regeneration/check. Leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
